-- The launcher this repository is read with, and the only file `eliotw` reads. One line: the tag.
--
-- Read rather than built: this repository is polyglot and the compiler in it is Scala, so `mill` builds
-- it and always will. What the launcher is for here is seeing this package the way a *consumer* sees it
-- — `./eliotw roots test` prints the eight source roots the layers' `at` clauses resolve to, which is
-- the one check that the descriptor everybody else depends on says what it means to say.
--
-- Keeping the pin out of `eliot.pkg` is what lets the wrapper stay a dumb script — a shell loop over
-- lines is not a parser, and the wrapper has to work in a checkout no eliot has ever run in.
v0.1
